{"session_id":"fixture-session","transcript_path":"/fixture/transcript.jsonl","cwd":"/tmp/proj","scratchpad_dir":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-user-claude-glass/ba42dfb5-c5a6-4a73-a44f-b9f4312dd993/scratchpad","prompt_id":"d3c1fc7f-dc82-485d-b083-efad13827ca3","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","effort":{"level":"medium"},"hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"WebSearch","tool_input":{"query":"Chrome DevTools Protocol Page.startScreencast"},"tool_response":{"query":"Chrome DevTools Protocol Page.startScreencast","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01SyGxKYRmNKioyaZdvXsKiy","content":[{"title":"Background transparency in startScreencast screencastframes · Issue #162 · ChromeDevTools/devtools-protocol","url":"https://github.com/ChromeDevTools/devtools-protocol/issues/162"},{"title":"DevTools: add a protocol method to generate a video stream of the page [41353306] - Chromium","url":"https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=781117"},{"title":"How to do video recording on headless chrome | by Anchen | Medium","url":"https://medium.com/@anchen.li/how-to-do-video-recording-on-headless-chrome-966e10b1221"},{"title":"Chrome DevTools Protocol - Page domain","url":"https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/tot/Page/"},{"title":"Chrome DevTools Protocol: The Invisible Engine Behind All Browser Automation — Caminho Solo","url":"https://www.caminhosolo.com.br/en/2026/03/chrome-devtools-protocol-automation/"},{"title":"page package - github.com/chromedp/cdproto/page - Go Packages","url":"https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/chromedp/cdproto/page"},{"title":"Chrome DevTools Protocol","url":"https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/"},{"title":"puppeteer screen recorder","url":"https://github.com/axelboberg/puppeteer-screen-recorder?ref=pkgstats.com"},{"title":"github.com","url":"https://github.com/puppeteer/puppeteer/blob/6ee7139704d8fa9bbf8d11d0e332756ff039c4f6/new-docs/puppeteer.cdpsession.md"}]},"I found search results related to Chrome DevTools Protocol's `Page.startScreencast` method. Here's what I found:\n\n## Overview\n\n`Page.startScreencast` enables screenshot streaming — continuous streaming of browser frames via the protocol, which can be used to build live browser previews, record user sessions, and create product demos.\n\n## How It Works\n\nThe method produces compressed image data, which is delivered via the `screencastFrame` event. Each screencast frame includes base64-encoded compressed image data, screencast frame metadata, and a frame number (session ID).\n\n## Usage Example\n\nTo use it, you listen to the `Page.screencastFrame` event, write the frame data (which can be in JPEG or PNG format), acknowledge the frame with `Page.screencastFrameAck()`, and then call `Page.startScreencast()`.\n\n## Related Methods\n\nThe method is typically used alongside:\n- `Page.stopScreencast` - to stop capturing frames\n- `Page.screencastFrameAck` - to acknowledge receipt of each frame\n\nThe official Chrome DevTools Protocol documentation for this method is available at the [Chrome DevTools Protocol Page domain documentation](https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/tot/Page/)."],"durationSeconds":6.018916291999863,"searchCount":1},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AgXCMrp8DBTJXUoXRLdHtJ","duration_ms":6020}
